WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.604
Sara liked to think that her doll, Emily, could understand her.

2
00:00:06.605 --> 00:00:10.208
Sometimes it even looked like the doll was about to speak.

3
00:00:10.209 --> 00:00:15.786
But Emily never said anything, and Sara began to have doubts.

4
00:00:15.787 --> 00:00:25.467
One night Sara was cold and hungry. She needed someone to talk to.

5
00:00:25.468 --> 00:00:30.377
"I can't bear this," said the poor girl, shaking.

6
00:00:30.378 --> 00:00:35.147
"I know I'm going to die. I'm cold and wet and starving.

7
00:00:35.148 --> 00:00:37.820
I've walked miles and miles today.

8
00:00:37.821 --> 00:00:43.594
Miss Minchin was in a terrible mood, and I saw some girls sneering at my shabbiness.

9
00:00:43.595 --> 00:00:48.329
Everybody in the kitchen has scolded me from morning until night."

10
00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:54.693
Emily said nothing. Sara continued to tell the doll about her bad day.

11
00:00:54.694 --> 00:00:57.468
The cook had sent her on several errands.

12
00:00:57.469 --> 00:01:00.887
But Sara couldn't find the last thing on the list.

13
00:01:00.888 --> 00:01:04.425
So the cook refused to give Sara any supper.

14
00:01:04.426 --> 00:01:11.882
"And some men were watching me when my old shoes made me slip in the mud," Sara went on.

15
00:01:11.883 --> 00:01:15.992
"I was covered with mud, and they laughed at me!

16
00:01:15.993 --> 00:01:20.363
I'm still covered with mud, Emily. Do you hear me?"

17
00:01:20.364 --> 00:01:26.339
Emily just stared straight ahead with her glass eyes and unchanging expression.

18
00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:29.111
Suddenly Sara was filled with rage.

19
00:01:29.112 --> 00:01:33.302
She lifted a hand and knocked Emily to the floor.

20
00:01:33.303 --> 00:01:39.963
Then she burst into tears, sobbing loudly.

21
00:01:39.964 --> 00:01:45.092
This was rare for Sara—the girl who never cried!

22
00:01:45.093 --> 00:01:49.389
"You're nothing but a doll !" shouted

23
00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:53.937
Sara. "You've never had a heart. You don't care about

24
00:01:53.938 --> 00:02:00.151
anyone!" Sara hid her face in her arms and

25
00:02:00.152 --> 00:02:03.973
sobbed. But after a while, she lifted her face and looked

26
00:02:03.974 --> 00:02:10.152
around. Emily was still lying upside down on the floor. Sara picked up the

27
00:02:10.153 --> 00:02:16.040
doll. "You can't help being a doll," Sara said. "You do your

28
00:02:16.041 --> 00:02:22.877
best." Sara kissed Emily and put the doll back. "I'm very sorry,

29
00:02:22.878 --> 00:02:28.458
Emily." Meanwhile Sara kept hoping that someone would move into the empty house next

30
00:02:28.459 --> 00:02:32.711
door. The attic window of the house was very close to Sara's

31
00:02:32.712 --> 00:02:38.600
window. "It would be so nice to see someone pop up from the window one day," she

32
00:02:38.601 --> 00:02:46.437
thought. "I could begin by greeting the person, and then all kinds of good things might

33
00:02:46.438 --> 00:02:51.810
happen!" One morning after finishing some errands, Sara turned the

34
00:02:51.811 --> 00:02:56.586
corner. To her great delight, she saw a moving van in front of the house!

35
00:02:56.587 --> 00:03:02.894
Men were going in and out of the house, carrying furniture and heavy packages.

36
00:03:02.895 --> 00:03:06.234
"Someone has bought the house!" she exclaimed.

37
00:03:06.235 --> 00:03:10.668
"Oh, I do hope someone nice will peek out the attic window."

38
00:03:10.669 --> 00:03:15.250
She wanted to watch the movers carrying everything inside.

39
00:03:15.251 --> 00:03:22.165
But she knew the cook would be angry if she stayed outside.

40
00:03:22.166 --> 00:03:29.399
"I remember thinking that Miss Minchin's tables and chairs looked just like her," said Sara.

41
00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:37.135
"And the Large family probably has furniture that looks like them—warm and cheerful armchairs and sofas.

42
00:03:37.136 --> 00:03:43.917
I wonder what I can learn about the new family from their things."

43
00:03:43.918 --> 00:03:47.843
Later in the day, Sara was sent on another errand.

44
00:03:47.844 --> 00:03:51.767
The movers had put several pieces of furniture on the sidewalk.

45
00:03:51.768 --> 00:03:55.778
Sara noticed a beautiful table of carved wood.

46
00:03:55.779 --> 00:04:00.008
She saw a screen covered with rich embroidery.

47
00:04:00.009 --> 00:04:03.886
"These are beautiful things," said Sara.

48
00:04:03.887 --> 00:04:08.175
"I think the new neighbors are rich. I hope they're nice."

49
00:04:08.176 --> 00:04:12.512
Among the furniture was a lovely statue of Buddha.

50
00:04:12.513 --> 00:04:16.823
"Someone in the family must have lived in India," said Sara.

51
00:04:16.824 --> 00:04:22.529
"I lived in India. I feel like we're friends already."

52
00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:28.788
When she returned, Sara saw a handsome man with rosy cheeks enter the house next door.

53
00:04:28.789 --> 00:04:31.757
It was the father from the Large family!

54
00:04:31.758 --> 00:04:35.318
This made her new neighbors even more interesting.

55
00:04:35.319 --> 00:04:40.924
The father soon came out again and gave some orders to the movers.

56
00:04:40.925 --> 00:04:44.854
That night Becky came to Sara's room.

57
00:04:44.855 --> 00:04:48.029
She had a bit of news about the new neighbors.

58
00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:53.762
"The owner of the house is an Englishman who lived in India," she told Sara.

59
00:04:53.763 --> 00:04:57.339
"He's very wealthy, and Mr. Large is his lawyer.

60
00:04:57.340 --> 00:05:01.354
The owner has had lots of troubles, and now he's sick."

61
00:05:01.355 --> 00:05:06.220
Sara nodded, listening carefully.

62
00:05:06.221 --> 00:05:11.024
A few weeks later, she saw Mr. Large and a nurse get out of a carriage.

63
00:05:11.025 --> 00:05:15.974
Two male servants came down the front steps of the house next door.

64
00:05:15.975 --> 00:05:19.624
They helped a pale, thin man out of the carriage.

65
00:05:19.625 --> 00:05:26.869
His face was narrow and pained, and he was wrapped in fur.

66
00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:33.526
The male servants carried him up the steps of the house, and soon afterward a doctor arrived.

67
00:05:33.527 --> 00:05:37.124
"He's very ill," thought Sara.

68
00:05:37.125 --> 00:05:44.416
And that was all she knew about the Englishman from India.

